module gunbc.integration_concern.h11ssl_unit3_hand_staged_edge_artifacts_have_no_place_in_the_edge_model

// One row of the integration-concern register. The roster derives the row from this file (module gunbc.integration_concern.roster);
// there is no list to append to. Ported from main's block in gunbc.integration_concern
// at this merge.

import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import std.content_hash { Sha256Digest, Sha256DigestHex }
import gunbc.integration_concern { CitesArtifact, CitesDeclaration, ConcernSighting, Integrated, IntegrationConcern, IntegrationEvidence, Open, RequirementEstablished, RetainedExecutionResult, SuspectedCapabilityGap, edge_install_residue_fold_integrated_revision, edge_residue_read_revision, h11ssl_unit3_edge_gate_refusal_revision, h11ssl_unit3_edge_live_read_revision, h11ssl_unit3_intake_sighting_revision }

// THE HAND-INSTALLED H11SSL-i (unit 3, BMC at 192.168.1.249): WHAT THE HAND WORK LEFT OUTSIDE THE
// MODEL. Sighted 2026-11-15 while bringing this unit under the modeled lifecycle. The operator
// installed its OS by hand from srv4's PXE edge -- a hand-staged install entry, a hand-staged seed and
// a hand-added dnsmasq line -- so the machine exists and runs, and three things about how it came to
// exist have no place in the model. Each row below is one of them, recorded as a gap in the model that
// could not express it, not as a defect in the hand work: the operator did what was needed at the
// bench, and the model is what is short of a standing.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The main revision the operator's reach report was received against (2026-11-16). The commit that
// carries the sighting below is a descendant of this one; the revision recorded is the tree the report
// was read against, not the sha of the commit that writes it down, which does not exist yet.
// The main revision the edge gate was found refusing a branch dispatch against: the session branch head
// the read-only edge observation was dispatched from, and refused at.
// The head review 96009 read when it surfaced the build-pool reservation as a second answer to "which
// hosts hold a build slot" (2026-11-17). The revision recorded is the tree that review read, not the sha
// of the commit that writes this sighting down, which does not exist yet.
// The reading at which the sold srv9 endpoint declaration still stood at 192.168.1.236 while the 2026-10-10
// Group B sale already recorded that unit as sold. This branch retires the declaration; the sighting names the
// commit the retirement was authored against, so the before-state stays checkable.
// The head that carries the build-pool carve rule (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired), read when the fork above was
// closed. As with the other rows here, the revision is the tree that was read, not the sha of the commit that
// writes this down.
// The MAIN revision the read-only edge observation ran against -- the ref the observe was dispatched at,
// and therefore the model state its readings are a statement about.
// THE EDGE MODEL RENDERS THE EDGE, SO IT CANNOT NAME WHAT WAS STAGED BESIDE IT.
data h11ssl_unit3_hand_staged_edge_artifacts_have_no_place_in_the_edge_model: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "h11ssl_unit3_hand_staged_edge_artifacts_have_no_place_in_the_edge_model",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_pinned_members"),
    requirement: "srv4's PXE edge carries artifacts that were staged by hand for this unit's install -- a seed, a dnsmasq line and an install entry -- and they must be retired by a converge run, not by a hand edit. The live observation of 2026-11-16 established the FILE half is already modelled: the converge computes a stale set (site_pxe_edge_stale_install_paths -- every file under the owned install roots that no model-rendered member produces) and an apply removes it one file at a time (site_pxe_edge_remove_stale), refusing at the first path that fails; srv4 put this unit's hand-staged seed in that set. The unmodelled half, which stands: state the edge carries that is NOT a file under an owned root has no representation at all. A hand-added dnsmasq line shows up only as file ... before=differs, with no line-level delta anyone can read from the model, and this unit's hand-staged install entry sat outside every family the fold claims, so the model could not say where it lived or that removing it was the converge's job. The ENTRY half is drawn in by the change this row now carries a sighting for: site_pxe_edge_owned_install_path takes the edge's staging/ subtree as a whole, derived from site_pxe_edge_served_root rather than from a second constant naming the same directory, and site_pxe_edge_empty_owned_install_dirs retires a directory the removal has emptied, inside the owned families only. That closes every artifact this requirement names by hand: the seed pair and srv15's install file were already in the fold's stale set and went there on 2026-11-18, the dnsmasq line went because the model RENDERS that whole config file and the same run reported before=differs outcome=written-and-read-back on it, and the install entry now sits inside the owned set. Two things are deliberately NOT recorded as this requirement standing unmet. The EFFECT on the host -- the staged file and the empty directories still have to be removed by an apply, which goes out only on a fleet-converge dispatch the operator authorizes -- is an execution owed, and it is carried as such by gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation::supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_edge_residue_2026_11_19 and its read obligation, not as a modelling gap here. And the reporting-granularity question raised above (a rendered file shows only before=differs, never which line changed) is a DIFFERENT capability: nothing about it leaves a hand-placed artifact out of the converge's reach, since the model owns the file, which is exactly why the line went away. It is stated here so the record keeps it, not as a half this requirement still fails. One constraint binds applies on this edge, and it is a lane instruction rather than a fact about the edge, so it is stated as what it is and claims no authority it does not have: smart-crane-730 held this lane's apply against srv4 on 2026-11-16, inside the site PXE edge bring-up plan that is his lane, until srv15's install binding is admitted on this edge. The fact underneath it comes from this repository, not from the operator -- gunbc.machine_intake.srv15_host_nic_observation records 9c:6b:00:e7:ca:63 as srv15's install NIC, and three of the five stale paths the observe listed are named for that MAC. gunbc.design_ruling carries dated OPERATOR rulings, so the hold is not entered there; the bring-up plan carrier carries it on its side."
    standing: RequirementEstablished {
      by: CitesArtifact {
        label: "artifacts/receipts/site-pxe-edge-observe-main-run-43789720870-2026-11-16/observe_wire_lines.txt (srv4's own answers: stale-install-files=found naming this unit's seed paths; dnsmasq config before=differs; nothing written)",
        sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "7f3956a28b3b07223163d0f868d7fabb5b4c51c1633d5ce8384eda6c2801f415" as Sha256DigestHex },
      },
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_pinned_members"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_config_path"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_tftp_root"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_stale_install_paths"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_remove_stale"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_install_nic_mac"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_owned_install_path"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_empty_owned_install_dirs"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_edge_residue_2026_11_19"),
    ],
  },
  question: "The stale fold owns files under the edge's install roots. What owns the live state that is not such a file -- a dnsmasq line the model never rendered, an install entry that is not in the roots the fold lists -- and what does a converge run have to read before it removes one?",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: h11ssl_unit3_intake_sighting_revision,
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesArtifact {
          label: "artifacts/host-observations/h11ssl-unit3-lan-read-2026-11-15/lan_read_2026-11-15.txt (the unit's network sightings; the hand install route is what put them on the LAN)",
          sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "a5500a7c1bfd9528d4284532569e2d15eb48a991eb15a9280ed5df39e97be6cb" as Sha256DigestHex },
        },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_ipmi_pxe_boot_path_standing"),
          },
        ],
      },
      account: "Sighted by still-fox-404 on 2026-11-15 while modeling this unit's intake. The unit's OS came up from a hand-staged install entry, seed and dnsmasq line on srv4; the edge model renders only the members it pins, so nothing in the model names those three artifacts and a converge run cannot be shown what it is about to remove. Nothing on srv4 was read or changed by this lane, and the retire step is owed through site_pxe_edge_converge, never by hand.",
    },
    tail: [
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: h11ssl_unit3_edge_gate_refusal_revision,
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesArtifact {
            label: "artifacts/receipts/site-pxe-edge-observe-branch-ref-refusal-2026-11-16/wif_refusal_log_excerpt.txt (fleet-converge workflow run 43786925157: the workload-identity gate refused the READ-ONLY edge observation at a branch ref)",
            sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "ecdaa1a1a535c5c8eba5651632dffea469021dc04e5b792df370fe7fe01feac7" as Sha256DigestHex },
          },
          tail: [],
        },
        account: "Sighted by still-fox-404 on 2026-11-16, second sighting of the SAME concern, and it deepens rather than repeats it: the obstacle is not only that the model cannot show the converge what to delete, but that a session branch cannot even LOOK. Dispatching the read-only observation of srv4's pinned edge (mode site_pxe_edge_observe) from a session branch was refused by the workflow's own workload-identity gate before it reached srv4 -- auth.branch_run_grant grants a run-scoped account only after THAT run's branch-run grant, and this mode has no such grant for a branch dispatch. So the read-only diff that must precede any retirement can only be produced at main (or after brokering a grant for the branch run), which means the evidence a cleanup needs is structurally out of reach of the branch that owes the cleanup. This is not specific to this unit: every host this lifecycle brings up inherits it.",
      },
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: h11ssl_unit3_edge_live_read_revision,
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesArtifact {
            label: "artifacts/receipts/site-pxe-edge-observe-main-run-43789720870-2026-11-16/observe_wire_lines.txt (the observe entry's own wire block from srv4, workflow run 43789720870, dispatched at main; the README beside it bounds what it shows)",
            sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "7f3956a28b3b07223163d0f868d7fabb5b4c51c1633d5ce8384eda6c2801f415" as Sha256DigestHex },
          },
          tail: [
            CitesDeclaration {
              declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_edge_sighting"),
            },
          ],
        },
        account: "Sighted by still-fox-404 on 2026-11-16, third sighting, and it CORRECTS the first one -- which is why it is appended rather than edited in. The first sighting said nothing in the model names the hand-staged artifacts. That is wrong for the file half. The live observation (dispatched at main after the refusal below, and it DID reach srv4 with a model-materialized known-hosts anchor) computes a stale set of exactly this kind -- site_pxe_edge_stale_install_paths: every file under the owned install roots that no model-rendered member produces -- and an apply removes that set file by file (site_pxe_edge_remove_stale), refusing at the first path that fails. srv4's own answer put this unit's hand-staged seed in that set: stale-install-files=found listed /srv/gunbc-site-pxe-edge/http/seed/ac-1f-6b-e6-75-eb/user-data and .../meta-data under a directory named for this unit's install NIC, outcome StaleLeftObserveOnly because the mode is read-only. So the model DOES have a place for a hand-staged file: it is computed from the live listing, not kept as a ledger row. What survives of the concern is narrower and still open: (a) the hand-staged dnsmasq LINE is not a file under an owned root, and the observe can report only before=differs for the config -- never which lines the live file carries extra -- so the non-file half of live-but-unrendered edge state has no representation; (b) this unit's hand-staged install ENTRY is NOT among the five stale paths (the only install cfg listed is 9c:6b:00:e7:ca:63's), so either it lives somewhere the stale fold does not own or it is already gone, and no read yet says which; (c) nothing was removed because the mode is read-only (outcome StaleLeftObserveOnly, placement not-attempted) -- NOT because a refusal stopped it: that verdict comes from site_pxe_edge_run_succeeded's ObserveOnly arm refusing while the Aarch64 chain is withheld for a member whose digest leg could not run, and an apply is not refused for that reason (the withheld-member concern beside this one carries the correction, and the code read that settled it).",
      },
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: h11ssl_unit3_edge_live_read_revision,
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.srv15_host_nic_observation", decl_name: "srv15_host_nic_mac"),
          },
          tail: [
            CitesArtifact {
              label: "artifacts/receipts/site-pxe-edge-observe-main-run-43789720870-2026-11-16/observe_wire_lines.txt (stale-install-files=found lists the three 9c-6b-00-e7-ca-63 paths beside this unit's two)",
              sha256: Sha256Digest { hex: "7f3956a28b3b07223163d0f868d7fabb5b4c51c1633d5ce8384eda6c2801f415" as Sha256DigestHex },
            },
          ],
        },
        account: "Sighted on 2026-11-16 by still-fox-404 at smart-crane-730's instruction, and it is why this lane holds its own apply even though its read is done. Three of the five stale paths the observe listed are not this unit's: they carry 9c:6b:00:e7:ca:63, which gunbc.machine_intake.srv15_host_nic_observation records as SRV15's install NIC. So one stale set spans two hosts and two lanes -- the files this bring-up wants removed, and the hand-staged install entry and seed that srv15's arrival (the lane of #16357) targets. Deleting them before that lane admits its own binding would be a converge acting on a host whose model is mid-flight, and that is exactly what the stale fold cannot see: it computes staleness per edge, not per host's lifecycle stage. The hold is smart-crane-730's instruction inside his own bring-up-plan lane. It is NOT entered in gunbc.design_ruling: that ledger carries dated rulings of the operator, and nobody gave this one operator authority -- the MAC-to-srv15 fact it rests on is this repository's own record (gunbc.machine_intake.srv15_host_nic_observation), read here by a read-only observe. Held CONDITIONAL, per smart-crane-730, and not to be chased: the stale set is 'install files no admitted binding renders', so those three paths leave the stale set iff the install binding admitted on this edge renders exactly those paths; if the render lands elsewhere, they stay stale and the hand-staged files stay on the box. Whether they land at those three paths is a property of the render, not of any lane's intent -- and proud-badger's arrival renders nothing on this edge, so that is not the question to ask anyone. Nothing here says the render does or does not name them.",
      },
      ConcernSighting {
        revision: edge_residue_read_revision,
        evidence: FreeSemigroup {
          head: CitesDeclaration {
            declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.machine_intake.supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_intake_observation", decl_name: "supermicro_h11ssl_unit3_edge_residue_2026_11_19"),
          },
          tail: [
            CitesDeclaration {
              declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_remove_stale"),
            },
            CitesDeclaration {
              declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_revision_citation_that_no_landing_contains", decl_name: "a_revision_citation_that_no_landing_contains"),
            },
          ],
        },
        account: "Read off srv4 read-only on 2026-11-19T20:55Z and again on 2026-11-20T06:19:53Z, and attributed to the fold by its OWN LOG rather than by mtimes. TWO OF THE THREE HAND-STAGED ARTIFACTS ARE ALREADY GONE, BY THE CONVERGE: fleet-converge run 44249605412 (dispatched 2026-11-18T06:12:13Z at head 418bf0a167) prints at 06:29:46.827Z stale-install-files=removed: over five paths -- this unit's seed user-data and meta-data, srv15's seed pair, and srv15's install config -- and in the same run, file dnsmasq-proxy-dhcp-config path=/etc/gunbc-site-pxe-edge.dnsmasq.conf before=differs outcome=written-and-read-back, which is what took the hand-added ken line out of the proxy config: the file now carries three dhcp-host lines and none of them names this unit's install MAC. THE THIRD SURVIVES BOTH READS: /srv/gunbc-site-pxe-edge/staging/withdrawn-h11new/ac:1f:6b:e6:75:eb.cfg, 450 bytes, whose own header reads hand-staged 2026-11-15 (session 9a3ff854): one-shot autoinstall of the new H11SSL at BMC 192.168.1.249; remove after install, and which still carries a live autoinstall stanza naming srv4's installer image and seed URLs. It sits outside every family the owned-path predicate claims, and that run's log never contains h11new or withdrawn -- the fold has never listed it. The second read adds what a file-only rule cannot see at all: the directories the removal left empty -- http/seed/ac-1f-6b-e6-75-eb and http/seed/9c-6b-00-e7-ca-63, both emptied by that run at 06:29:46Z, http/seed/9c-6b-00-e7-ca-9c, empty since 2026-11-10, and tftp/grub/install. DIRECTION is settled by smart-crane-730's ruling of 2026-11-19, relayed to this session: draw the owned set from WHAT THE FOLD RENDERS, not from the name somebody gave a directory -- the fold renders nothing under the served root's staging/ subtree, so anything found there is residue by construction -- and refuse to model withdrawn-*, which is one person's naming convention and would mint vocabulary for a hand act. The change rides in this row's own diff: the staging subtree joins the owned roots through site_pxe_edge_served_root, and site_pxe_edge_empty_owned_install_dirs retires a directory the removal has emptied, inside the owned families only, deepest first. The ordering that change depends on is stated where it can be read rather than assumed: the placement leg stages the installer image under that same subtree, verifies it by digest and un-stages it inside one leg, and the run takes that leg BEFORE the stale listing; the witness pins the order the run reports, and if the order ever flipped the cost is a re-download verified by digest again, never a corrupted served copy. WHAT KEEPS THIS ROW OPEN is the dnsmasq half quoted in the requirement -- a line-level delta the model cannot read -- plus the removal on srv4 itself, which happens only through a fleet-converge dispatch the operator authorizes (nothing is dispatched from this lane) and the re-read afterwards that turns the read obligation into a receipt. The DISPOSITION stays Open deliberately even though the ownership change rides in the same diff: closing it would need an integrated_at naming a revision that already contains the new fold, and no such revision exists until this lands -- the invalid state gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_revision_citation_that_no_landing_contains files. The closure goes to a follow-up that can name the landing revision, the way h11ssl_unit3_three_gpu_functions_against_two_reported_cards did.",
      },
    ],
  },
  disposition: Integrated {
    evidence: IntegrationEvidence {
      integrated_at: edge_install_residue_fold_integrated_revision,
      // Nothing is deleted to close this row: the fold grew, so no declaration was superseded. The pre-change state
      // lives on in the row's fifth sighting, which records the residue as it stood when the fold could not reach it.
      superseded: [],
      replacement: FreeSemigroup {
        head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_owned_install_path"),
        tail: [
          decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_owned_install_roots"),
          decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_served_root"),
          decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_empty_owned_install_dirs"),
          decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge", decl_name: "site_pxe_edge_stale_install_files"),
        ],
      },
      executions: FreeSemigroup {
        head: RetainedExecutionResult {
          control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge_witness", decl_name: "a_hand_staged_entry_under_the_edge_staging_subtree_is_stale"),
          run: "green at ca0b9c46b3d1 (the landed pull request's head, an ancestor of 6f1e4de1eac8) inside test.claim.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge_witness: 108 claims, 108 pass, 0 fail, clean tree, claim_batch sha256 b569513e8ffcb5ca884647e8de81df2fde2cecdfbdfa537068e75fc4b0453934 built from fb2127fc88f8; local serial, one claim_batch at a time. RED as a planted pair, each reverted in place: with the staging root removed from site_pxe_edge_owned_install_roots this claim fails (3 claims run: pass=1 fail=2).",
          conclusion: "The hand-staged install entry under the edge's staging/ subtree is inside the set the fold claims, so the converge lists it as residue and can remove it. Drop that ownership arm and it is invisible to the fold -- which is exactly the half this row carried open.",
        },
        tail: [
          RetainedExecutionResult {
            control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge_witness", decl_name: "a_directory_emptied_by_the_withdrawal_is_pruned_and_the_family_roots_stay"),
            run: "same batch, same binary, same revision as the entry claim above. RED twice, each reverted in place: with the staging root dropped (pass=1 fail=2), and with site_pxe_edge_ancestor_directories returning no ancestors (pass=2 fail=1) -- the second plant is the one that shows the protection walk is load-bearing, since without it the seed directory this run renders into lands on the prune list.",
            conclusion: "A directory a completed removal has emptied is retired, inside the owned families only, deepest first, while each family root and every directory the fold keeps or renders content into is protected.",
          },
          RetainedExecutionResult {
            control: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.fleet.site_pxe_edge_converge_witness", decl_name: "a_refused_directory_removal_refuses_the_apply"),
            run: "same batch, same binary, same revision; green, and it stays green under both plants, which is the correct shape -- it tests the apply's failure path, not which roots are owned.",
            conclusion: "An apply that cannot remove an emptied directory fails rather than reporting success, so a partially pruned edge can never read as a clean one.",
          },
        ],
      },
    },
  },
}
